			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize UriComponents IPC marshalling helpers\n\nDecompose the monolithic `Source/IPC/UriComponents.rs` into a flat module tree to align with the distributed architecture's 'one export per file' pattern. Each logical unit (`MID_URI`, `StampMidUri`, `FromFilePath`, `FromUrl`, `Normalize`) is now its own PascalCase unit file, exposing the public API via the root manifest.\n\nThe documentation has been expanded to clarify the VS Code IPC reviver requirements (`$mid === 1`) and the consequences of missing tags. This reorganization reduces file complexity, enforces strict PascalCase naming for all exports, and prepares the IPC layer for finer-grained testing of URI marshalling logic within the Mountain backend.",
			"SHA": "bd60b172ef9394d2f2d10a985fb95701269e9cad"
		}
